Subject: [PATCH] playerbots: a grind spot that keeps killing a bot is not picked again

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS

NewRpgBaseAction::SelectRandomGrindPos picks any cached grind spot of the bot's
level inside 2500 yards, and nothing it has done before is remembered. A bot
that dies on a spot therefore goes straight back to it, and to the road to it.

Measured on the dev realm over three days from overseer_death, for the 37
guild lineup characters below level 50 that run on this picker (88 percent of
their deaths are ungrouped, out of any dungeon, with the bot on its own
autonomous status): 2,386 overworld deaths, of which 1,175 (49 percent) were
within 150 yards of an earlier death of the same character in the preceding six
hours, 678 (28 percent) had two or more such earlier deaths, and 415 (17
percent) had three or more. One level 35 character died 45 times inside a
single 100 yard square on the road past a hostile capital's guards (level 75),
roughly hourly, and another 27 times at a hostile outpost. Their zones are not
the problem: the killers' mean level was the character's own.

WHAT IT DOES

NewRpgInfo gains a NewRpgDeathMemory: where this bot died, in memory, newest 24
kept, six hours long. AutoReleaseSpiritAction and ReleaseSpiritAction record
the spot through IncrementDeathCount (battleground deaths are skipped there
already). Two deaths within 150 yards make that ground hot for this bot.
SelectRandomGrindPos skips a spot that is on hot ground, or whose straight line
from the bot passes within 100 yards of it (a bot standing on hot ground is
only refused spots on it, so it can walk out). Only when that leaves no spot at
all is the rule dropped, so the memory never strands a bot. No bot is moved by
anything but its own pick, and no XP, level, gold or item is granted.

WHAT IT DOES NOT DO

It does not touch quest points, camps or wander picks, and the straight line is
an approximation of the road. A restart forgets the memory.

WHAT WOULD LET THIS PATCH BE DELETED

An upstream grind picker that weighs recent deaths, or that avoids ground
guarded by creatures hostile to the bot's team.

APPLIES TO

  repo: https://github.com/quadseven/mod-playerbots.git
  SHA:  40884e9c135c1daf27ffd894a6047502a5701130 (the pin), after patches
        0001 to 0027 of this directory. It touches NewRpgInfo.h,
        NewRpgBaseAction.cpp (SelectRandomGrindPos) and ReleaseSpiritAction.cpp
        (IncrementDeathCount).

